    "done_when": "Lead decision centroid-row-definition = first-moments-derived-tolerance (plan centroid-constrained-oracle-solve, recorded at 3c026a156). Today ForwardProfile.current_moment_observation (nova/equilibrium/forward.py:1238-1261) hands observe_current_moments (nova/equilibrium/observation.py:279) only cell currents at cell centres, so CurrentCentroidConstraint (nova/equilibrium/constraint.py:934) places the exact analytic state 6.17 mm off its continuous target at 135 cells; adding each cell's within-cell first moment recovers 98.75 percent of that (/home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/nova/s22/cco-root-cause-centroid-moment-contract.md, merged 96d8d4c46). (1) Move the first-moment recovery that benchmarks/plasma_cell_map_fidelity.py performs (recover_physical_first_moments and current_centroid) into the library, make the centroid observation the row reads use it, and keep the computation differentiable. (2) The row's clause becomes a discretisation tolerance: the analytic state's own first-moment centroid residual at the row's resolution, computed by the same row code and recorded with the row (in scripts/analytic_oracle_fixtures/centroid_row.py), replacing the fixed 1e-12-pitch clause for analytic-fixture rows; a test asserts that the analytic state passes it and that a state displaced by twice that residual fails. (3) A test pins the first-moment centroid of the analytic weak-rotation-reactor-static -110 state at 135 cells within its recorded tolerance of the continuous target (the measured residual was 77 micrometres). (4) No solve and no H200 job in this node; the constrained re-measure waits for both derivative repairs. Pass clip_mode='exact' explicitly anywhere a mode is needed; the process-global mode no longer exists. Gate: JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu pytest of tests/test_forward_constraints.py and the new test file, in place on the fleet allocation, delta against the parent; a baseline arm extracts only the subtrees it imports and removes them before the manifest. Report at /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/nova/s22/cco-first-moment-centroid-row.md, with any other caller of CurrentCentroidConstraint whose behaviour changes listed.",
